README – Replication package for Blow and Crawford




  README – Replication package for Blow and
  Crawford, "Nonparametric Analysis of
  Reference-Dependent Preferences"
    Oct 22, 2026         · ​@Laura


  Overview
  This package reproduces every table, figure and computed number in the main paper and
  Supplemental Appendix of Laura Blow and Vincent P. Crawford, "Nonparametric Analysis
  of Reference-Dependent Preferences", from the raw data. All code is in R. One file runs
  everything: code/00_run_all.R .

       Default run (shipped results): under a minute. The package ships the estimation
       results and the Table A5 sweep results, so the default run rebuilds every exhibit from
       them and checks key numbers against the printed paper.
       Full run from scratch: about 3 days on a standard laptop: about 37 hours for the
       estimation and about 37 hours for the Table A5 sweep. Both can be interrupted and
       resumed.

  Figures 1-5 and A1-A2 are theoretical schematics drawn by hand; no data or code
  produces them.


  Data availability and provenance
  The analysis uses two raw data files, both publicly available and both included in
  data_raw/ . The taxi data are posted in the American Economic Association's replication
  archives (Farber 2008a; Crawford and Meng 2011a), and we include a copy with
  attribution. The CPI data are published by the US Bureau of Labor Statistics and are in the
  public domain.




