  Taxi data. Henry Farber's trip sheets for 21 drivers, the sample of Farber (2005). The
  dataset is publicly posted in Farber's (2008) replication package and again in Crawford
  and Meng's (2011), both now distributed through openICPSR (DOIs in References).
   taxi015.dta is the authors' copy of this dataset. The code aggregates trips to driver-
  days and uses the variables id , date , fare , tripmin , brmin , waitmin , rainfall ,
  snowfall , shift , mintemp and maxtemp . taxi015.csv is a plain-text copy of
   taxi015.dta , provided because the Stata format is proprietary; the code reads the .dta
  file.

  CPI data. Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U), all items, New York-
  Newark-Jersey City, NY-NJ-PA, monthly, not seasonally adjusted (BLS series
  CUURS12ASA0), months from 1999 to 2001, downloaded from
  https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CUURS12ASA0 (file dated June 2018). The code divides
  each driver-day's earnings by the index for that month, normalised to the sixth month in
  the file.


  Computational requirements
  Software. R 4.3.1 on Windows 11 (64-bit), with these packages (versions used):




