  Shipped results. output/data/ contains the estimation results, one file per dimension of
  reference dependence: Areas (Both) ... , Areas (Earnings) ... and Areas (Hours)
  ... , each ending NestedGeneralU.intervals_24_D1000_LPt20_scaled_slope1e-
  04_final.Rdata . output/data/tuning/ contains the Table A5 sweep, one file per grid
  setting plus the WARP verdicts. These are what the paper reports. They let the default
  run finish in under a minute; the from-scratch runs regenerate them.


  Instructions to replicators
  Default run (under a minute).

   1. Install R and the four packages listed under Computational requirements.
   2. Unzip the package. Open code/00_run_all.R and set project_root , near the top, to
       the folder that contains code/ , data_raw/ and output/ . Use forward slashes, even
       on Windows.
   3. Run the whole file (in RStudio: Source). Leave the switches at their defaults:
        RUN_ESTIMATION <- FALSE , RUN_TABLE_A5 <- TRUE .



                                                                                                      Page 5 of 9
README – Replication package for Blow and Crawford




   4. Figures are written to output/pics/ and tables to output/data/ . Everything printed
       is also saved in output/run_all_log.txt . The self-checks print, among other lines,
       "ALL 168 CELLS MATCH the printed Table A1" and "Section 5.6 reproduced exactly".

  Full run from scratch (about 3 days).

   1. Move the three shipped Areas (...) files out of output/data/ and move the
        output/data/tuning/ folder out of the package, for example into a backup folder.
   2. In 00_run_all.R , set RUN_ESTIMATION <- TRUE (and keep RUN_TABLE_A5 <- TRUE ).
   3. Run the whole file. It runs the estimation (about 37 hours), then the Table A5 sweep
      (about 37 hours), then all the exhibits.

  If a run is interrupted (a forced restart, a flat battery), run 00_run_all.R again
  unchanged. The estimation and the Table A5 sweep both save their results after every
  driver and resume from the last finished driver; the driver in progress starts again. Each
  restart writes a fresh run_all_log.txt . Keep the computer plugged in and set not to
  sleep.


  List of exhibits and the code that produces them
  Every exhibit and computed number in the paper maps to one script. Figures are in
  output/pics/ , tables in output/data/ ; numbers quoted in the text are also printed in
   output/run_all_log.txt . [tag] stands for
   intervals_24_D1000_LPt20_scaled_slope1e-04_final .

